KG42.register("clusters-bcd45a7004bde05048fc98e8",{"id":"10-hierarchical_coordination::v142-d-K003","paper":"10-hierarchical_coordination","label":"Maximization of Traded Energy and Counterparty Allocation under Strategy Two","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K003","label":"Maximization of Traded Energy and Counterparty Allocation under Strategy Two","market_meaning":"When Strategy Two is selected, the LMO coordinates counterparties based on submitted supply offers and demand bids and determines allocation by maximizing total P2P electricity sales. The source references feasibility constraints with the same numbers as those in Strategy One, but the existing M03 chains have not yet provided complete object instances and bindings for these constraints.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01","v141-a-M02","v141-a-M03"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","coordination","clearing","matching"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"R014 and R015 jointly represent Strategy Two in M03; R008 and R010 provide only the case submission procedure that the original text explicitly states applies to both strategies. R009 shares only an interface for consulting the constraint family, and R004 serves only as general background; the Strategy One objective and its solution results do not become conditions for Strategy Two.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Strategy Two and Strategy One have different decision objectives and therefore remain separate Rule-Clusters; this cluster brings together bid receipt, counterparty matching, and energy allocation, without merging the two strategies merely because they share the LMO or constraint numbers. Its scope is limited to quantity allocation, and the M02 pricing chain has not been expanded into M03 rules.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R014","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Represents traded energy maximization under Strategy Two and the LMO's allocation responsibility."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R015","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Adds the bid inputs and counterparty matching meaning of the same Strategy Two decision."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"shared","role":"context","rationale":"The general P2P matching description serves as background and does not add objectives or feasibility conditions to Strategy Two."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"shared","role":"support","rationale":"References the case requirement to submit only one type, which applies to both strategies, while retaining the case scope."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"shared","role":"support","rationale":"Only provides access to Eqs. (16) to (23), represented by C002, C003, and C007 to C010; the Strategy One objective, decision instances, and allocation results are not shared."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"References the common procedure in the case for submitting curves to the LMO according to buyer or seller status."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R015","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R014","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R015::phi::v141-c-R015-C001","v141-c-R015::phi::v141-c-R015-C002","v141-c-R015::phi::v141-c-R015-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C001","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e23"],"rationale":"The original M03 text uses the same optimization to explain matching between bids and determination of transaction quantities; combining the two chains can express the inputs, responsibility, and outputs of this decision."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R015","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R015::phi::v141-c-R015-C001","v141-c-R015::phi::v141-c-R015-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e34","v141-b-g02-e23"],"rationale":"The M02 case evidence explicitly states that this submission procedure serves either strategy, and the M03 evidence states that Strategy Two uses these bids for matching; the original mechanism identifiers of both pieces of evidence are retained."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e34"],"rationale":"Submission of only one type and the buyer or seller status conditions in the same case jointly define the input procedure; they are not rewritten as new mathematical constraints in M03."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R015","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R015::phi::v141-c-R015-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e23"],"rationale":"Strategy Two is a specific decision method for general LMO matching activities; shared background does not constitute a new dependency or a determination that the optimization is the same."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R014","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C003","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C007","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C008","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C009","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C010"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e23"],"rationale":"M03 explicitly references Eqs. (16) to (23), whose existing C representations are located in R009 of M02; this mapping provides an interface to the constraint provisions and does not identify M02 variable instances or optimal solutions as M03 objects."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R009::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R010::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R014::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R015::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e34"],"rationale":"The LMO functional node is shared, but the strategy and procedure scopes are retained separately; this is not used to merge the optimization problems."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R014::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e23"],"rationale":"All reference the local allocation function; decision instances and results under different objectives are not equal and cannot be mapped as the same quantity."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R008::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R009::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R010::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R015::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e34"],"rationale":"The demand submission function can be referenced across strategies; case conditions and strategy-specific input relationships are not merged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O04","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R008::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R009::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R010::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R015::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e34"],"rationale":"The supply submission function is the same, while each strategy's local constraints and evidence attribution are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O05","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::matching.counterparties","v141-c-R015::V::matching.counterparties"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e23"],"rationale":"General matching and Strategy Two matching reference the same functional node; the general procedure cannot be interpreted as a second Strategy Two optimization."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"M03 declares only the electricity sale quantity used in the objective and the feasible set specified by equation numbers; electricity purchase quantities, block allocations, transaction states, bid upper bounds, and their M03 bindings are not provided. Sharing R009 allows the provisions to be located, but does not yet confirm that the Strategy Two instance is complete and closed; the upper bounds imposed separately on counterparties also do not automatically provide aggregate quantity restrictions across counterparties.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R014","v141-c-R015","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R014::x::v141-c-R014-X001","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C002","v141-c-R015::phi::v141-c-R015-C003","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C003","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e23"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream work should specify the object instances, parameter roles, and bindings of the shared constraint family in M03 and check the treatment of capacity across counterparties; Strategy One results must not be copied, nor may constraints be added independently."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G02","category":"ontology_extension","description":"Strategy Two maximizes traded energy to improve community self-sufficiency; this is not equivalent to maximizing social welfare or the number of transactions. v141-b-g01-prop-ss remains an unapproved proposal.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R014","v141-c-R015"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e23"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop-ss"],"required_work":"Manually inspect the objective concept and the applicability of the proposal, retaining the current clearing.local and the original objective reference without replacing them with other objective nodes."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G03","category":"unverified_source","description":"Both sharing of the constraint family and the submission interface across mechanisms are based on unreviewed candidate citations; the evidence attribution of M02 and M03 remains unchanged, and these links do not establish source correctness or the scientific completeness of either strategy.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R010","v141-c-R014","v141-c-R015"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e34"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually inspect each chain and independently check the scope of applicability of the shared constraints, the objectives, and the evidence transcription; this round does not claim to have passed independent review."}]},"rule_refs":["10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R014","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R015","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R004","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R008","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R009","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R010"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","COMP-da34359f040da554","KG31-0645fab4a79eb10b","KG31-284fede6dbff2be2","KG31-71938ef56b613c45"]});
